A1. A foreign entanglement. ~ SPAGHETTI
A9. This has appealing eyes. ~ POTATO
A11. This has been done with a great deal of interest. ~ LOANED
A14. An indefinite article. ~ AN
A15. A disappointing word. ~ NO
A16. This will make any chicken lose her head. ~ AX
A17. This is quite a parent. ~ MA
A18. This one knows many tongues. (abbr.) ~ DR
A19. These stick to you all through life. ~ NAMES
A23. These two characters are from Missouri. ~ MO
A25. This is always hanging around the picture galleries. ~ ART
A27. This is what he does when he weakens. ~ RELENTS
A29. This can make her shut her mouth. ~ JAW
A30. Mamma deer. ~ DOE
A31. This describes the best kind of books, friends and wine. ~ OLD
A32. The uncertainty of woman. ~ AGE
A33. You cannot get much action from this kind of a pool. ~ STAGNANT
A36. What he did with his diamond to win her heart. ~ PLAYED
A38. An Anglo-Saxon slave. ~ ESNE
A39. These are always hanging on someone's neck in romantic Hawaii. ~ LEIS
A40. The kind of orders salesmen like to get. ~ REPEAT
A43. These tip the scales with much fat. ~ BUTCHERS
